      <div type="article" xml:id="PressMint-GB_1916-07-15_WidnesExaminer_art0005" n="art0005">
        <head>FOR SOLO AND SIDECAR</head>
        <p>FOR SOLO AND SIDECAR</p>
        <p>The "Save" that Satisfies.</p>
        <p>'Time was when people desirous of Saving some portion of their earnings were in doubt as to what to do with it and where to place it so- that it would be safe and get-at-able in case of need.</p>
        <p>Scotchmen, xvith that thrifty bias Which characterises them hi their Highland cots, and follows ''them to the wilds of Australia and if w backwoods of America, adaPted the idea of a Savings Bank.</p>
        <p>THE WARRINGTON, RUNCORN AND DISTRICT SAVINGS BANK, amongst the oldest of its kind in the kingdom, having been formed almost contemporary with others shortly after the Act of Parliament with the subject had been passed, 16th February, 1818.</p>
        <p>dealing</p>
        <p>was opened on</p>
        <p>The money deposited in the Ordinary Department of the Savings Bank has always been invested with the Government.</p>
        <p>Therefore Depositors, and all those boys and girls who are members of the School Penny Banks, formed under the auspices of the Savings have the pleasure and satisfaction in knowing that they are not only saving for themselves,, but are, at the same time, lending to ihe State their money, which will help to bring the War to a speedy, successful, and honourable end.</p>
        <p>Hank,</p>
        <p>Save to win the War and "the triumphant vindication of our cause."</p>
        <p>AT YOUR SERVICE:</p>
        <p>Warrington, Runcorn &amp; District Savings Bank.</p>
        <p>Established 1818.</p>
        <p>HEAD OFFICE</p>
        <p>- BUTTERMARKET STREET.</p>
        <p>BRANCHES -</p>
        <p>( BANK QUAY, 29, GREEN STREET. 1 EARLESTOWN, 5, QUEEN STREET.</p>
        <p>RUNCORN OFFICE</p>
        <p>44, 111611 STREET.</p>
        <p>!THE SAVINGS BANK is THE BANK FOR SAVINGS</p>
      </div>
