      <div type="article" xml:id="PressMint-GB_1916-07-15_WidnesExaminer_art0042" n="art0042">
        <head>Special First-aid Examination.</head>
        <p>Special First-aid Examination.</p>
        <p>• zaminer, Dr. Bowden. i•ProfiCiency Badge.—Miss Margaret Broadbent •meleroction owing to 12 months' service) and Miss -"°,,re R. Rumney. Advanced Certilicate.—The Misses Mary Bain- 13,„r1dge, J. Kathleen Bate, Marjorie Bennett, M., G. 14orney, Frances L. Green. Elsie P. Mason, J. E. kennie, Nora R. Rumney, Edith Mary Richardson, F. Clara A. Ilickell, Miss Ruby Witte and Miss niee Wright. Pleasing incident followed the presentation of 'eertificates, when Miss Broadbent handed to Dr. G. W. N. Joseph. lecturer on hygiene and sanita- t°2l. and Nurse Phillips, lecturer on home nursing, andsome evidences of appreciation by the etudents who profited by their great skill in these !..4biects. The gift to Dr. Joseph was a beautiful *liver salver, and that to Nurse Phillips, a valuable 'wristlet watch. A, Vecial programme is being arranged for the rtecoming session. In the autumn some lectures VI cookery will be given by the Director of Educe- is:Ha. and there will also be first-aid, nursing and 'Ygiene classes.</p>
