      <div type="article" xml:id="PressMint-GB_1916-07-15_WidnesExaminer_art0071" n="art0071">
        <p>BIRTHS, MARRIAGES, DEATHS.</p>
        <p>Notices of births, marriages, and deaths, in memoriam notices, and acknowledgments of sympathy are inserted in "The Examiner" at the following. rates :—Not exceeding 20 words, 1/0 each; every additional seven words, ed.</p>
        <p>Golden Wedding.</p>
        <p>GILBERT---dHASE.—On july 12th, 1866, at Toronto. Canada, by Rev. John Barclay, William Gilbert to Mary Elizabeth Chase. Present address: 10, Dickenson-street, Warrington.</p>
        <p>Deaths.</p>
        <p>ASH:rON.—Ny 10th, at 39. Cobden-street, James</p>
        <p>Ashton, aged-52 years. ATICINSON.—Mrs. Margaret Atkinson. 154, Lang- worthy-road, Seedley, late of Horwich and Bolton, died of motor accident it the Royal Infirmary, Manchester. Tuesday, 7uly 11th. 1916. Friends please accept this, the only, intimation. Inter- ment at Warrington.,</p>
        <p>RENNETT.—On July 12th, at 16, gank-street, Bolton, • Alice, the dearly loved daughter of Mrs. E. Martin, of 165,4 Winwick-road, Warriugton, aged 31 years.</p>
        <p>13RIpGE.—Ju1y 6th, at '2, Ashwood,-avenue, Thomas</p>
        <p>Bridge, aged-55 years. JOHNSON.—JuIy Bth, at 10, Firth-place, William ' Johnson, aged 58 years.</p>
        <p>LIGHTFOOT.—JuIy 13th, at 31b, Winwick-street Ralph Lightfoot, aged 56' years.</p>
        <p>In Memoriam.</p>
        <p>GARRATT.—In loving memory of James Edward Garratt, who died at Birmingham. July 3rd, 1915. From SISTER and BROTHERS. Winwick-road, Warrington.</p>
        <p>HIPKISS.—In loving memory of our dear son William Joseph (Willie), who died July lath, 1914 MR. and MRS. HIPKISS. 4, Lodge-lane, Warrington.</p>
        <p>NOR:TH.—In loving memory of Ernest Eli, who passed away July 13th. 1915. Gone, hut not forgotten by his Father and Mother. 142, Longford-street, Warrington.</p>
