        <head>To the Editor of "The Examiner."</head>
        <p>To the Editor of "The Examiner."</p>
        <p>"The Pearson and Knowles Coal and Iron Co., Limited, Warrington, July 13th, 1916. "Sir,—We thank you for your courtesy in sending us the advance proof of report of the meeting of the Warrington Trades and Labour Council,•ivhich is to appear in your next issue, relating to shortage of cottages in Warrington. We have no objection at all to our name appear- ing as ewners of the cottages referred to in the discussion, and in our opinion no comment is necessary from us upon what was actually said at the meeting. but it is, we think, better that</p>
