        <p>SERGEANT A. SPENCER Wounded.</p>
        <p>shire Fusiliers, who enlisted at the commence- ment of the war, has been wounded by shrapnel in the right breast. He is now in the Edin- burgh, War Hospital, and is making satisfactory progress. Sergeant Spencer, who is 28 years of age, formerly worked at the Mostyn Tube Works, Latchford, and was a member of the Warring- ton Athletic Club for many years. He was also a member of the Wycliffe P.S.A. SERGEANT W. FRANCIS. • Wounded In The Left Arm With Shrapnel. Sergeant William Francis, a married man, of 21, Pierpoint-street, and of the Royal Welsh Fusiliers, has been wounded with shrapnel in the let arm. A shell burst near him and several others, and all were buried. A piece of shell also cut in two the haversack belonging to Sergeant Francis. Sergeant Francis, who is 28 years of age, has been in the Army about eighteen months, and at the Front since November. He was formerly employed as an ironworker by the Pearson and Knowles Coal and Iron Co., Ltd. He is a native</p>
