        <p>having laboured indefatigably for its success. The club proudly boasts that it has never been in debt. Its initial expenses were cleared off by whist drives and other attractive functions, while the funds necessary to meet the big outlay in connection with the present grounds in 1913 were raised by the issue of a number of five per cent. shares. All these shares have now been redeemed. Though started for purely social purposes, the club ventured. prior to the war, into various com- petitions, and while not annexing many coveted trophies, showed that its members could acquit themselves most creditably upon the tennis field. In addition to the present President (Mr. W. H. Hartley), both Mr. J. W. Sanson (hon. sec.) and Mr. W. E. Booth (hon. treasurer), have been elected to their offices for the past five seasons. Mr. H. Shakeshaft is captain, and other members of the committee are: Mr. J. Swinton (now at the Front), Mr. H. Woodin and Mr. A. B. Starkey, while with Mrs. Kerfoot on the ladies' committee are Miss Jewkes, Mrs. Pharaoh and Miss Thomp- son. The members come from Stockton Heath. Lymm, Warrington and Padgate, as well as Grappenhall. CRICKET. TO-DAY'S MATCHES. WARRINGTON XI. v. NEWTON-LE-WILLOWS. This match will be played at Newton to-day, com- mencing at 2.30 P.m. Warrington (selected from): J. Constable (cap- tain), W. H. Bell, W. C. Brooks, T. E. Allen, W. Howard, F. Tole, G. Duckworth, G. Mann, W. Bennett, F. Lemon, F. Parr, B. Taylor and T. Knight. Train leaves Bank Quay Station at 1.54 p.m. Players meet at 1.45 p.m. Umpire, S. W. Holden. EMMANUEL CHURCH CRICKET CLUB v. CROSFIELD'S CRICKET CLUB. At Arpley ,to-day (Saturday), wickets pitched at 2.30 p.m. prompt. Team: T. Lloyd (captain), S. Banner, H. Berry, E. Harrison, S. Hughes, T. Hughes, A. Lees, G. Lloyd, A. Mather, J. Pownall, H. Wright. WARRINGTON XI. PROGRAMME. The recently formed Warrington XI. C.C. have now completed arrangements for this season, several attractive fixtures appearing in the list. All matches will be played away. Fixtures:— June 17.—Emmanuel Institute. Won. „ 24.—Earlestown 2nd. Won. July I.—Lymm Hospital. Won. „ B.—Earlestown 2nd: Cancelled. „ 15.—Newton-le-Willows. „ 22.—St. Helens Recs. „ 29.—Prescot. Aug. s.—Earlestown Ist. „ 7.—Liverpool Tram. „ B.—Flixton. „ Helens Recs. „ 19.—Lord Derby Military Hospital. „ 26.—Wallasey. Sept. 2.—Earlestown 2nd. „ 9.—Wallasey. „ 16.—Flixton. ANGLING. WARRINGTON WQRKING MEN'S ASSOCIATION. N.A. CENTRE. The only places that are fishing up to last year's form at present are the Runcorn end of the Bridge- water Canal; and Newbridge, above the Vale Royal Locks. Other places ...anglers have fished for all they were worth, but results have been very poor, the Shrop- shire Union Canal. the Gowy, and the Norton have all provided the same fate. From a dozen anglers at Norton there were not a dozen fish, and the most aggravating part of it was that there seemed to be plenty of fish about. They were rising almost all round as evening drew near. Whether it was the elements or not. can only be surmised. The best from the Gowy is Mr. J. Sherratt's gudgeon of loz. 10dr. Shropshire Union, beyond a few roach from soz. to 10oz.. there is nothing worth mentioning. The Weaver is quite a puzzle. Below the lock at Vale Royal there is practically nothing. An angler may sit all day and not get a catch. In I a match last Sunday 25 sat down for three hours, and the result was one fish, less than loz. Above the lock matters seem to be as usual. In a match last Sunday two members from Salford tied for first and second with the weight of 21b. 7oz. The way things are at present, secretaries must be having an anxious time about their matches. If there is a poor return the secretary is the first to hear all kinds of remarks, about taking the match to such a place, many forgetting that they themselves selected the spot at a general meeting in the early part of the year. As the contests are all close at hand let us hope that things will have a turn speedily. NOTICE. The Bay Horse opening contest takes place at Norton on Saturday. July 22nd. The Secretary will receive entries on Monday, 17th, and Friday, 21st.</p>
